{
  "_comment": "THE CONVERSATIONAL LOOP - PLAN 2x §3.3. The AI writes this file and bumps `rev`; the Texture panel polls /api/textureparams once a second and regenerates on a rev change. No websocket, no connection state, survives a page reload. `autoplay` is absent BY DESIGN - sound only ever on the composer SPACE or Play. Every label must NAME THE DIALS IT MOVED (§6 two-sided contract), so the qualitative interface never goes opaque.",
  "_slate": "rev 3 (2026-08-20, day 21) - THE CHARACTER x SPEED GRID. Four characters (Sm smear · Rn rain · Ga gallop · Gr groove) x four speeds (6 · 12 · 18 · 22 attacks/s) = 16 variants. WHY THIS SHAPE: the composer found that the model buttons and the variant tabs are two separate paths - any arrow press calls generate(), which reloads this.spec from the params file and DISCARDS the clicked model (texture_panel.js:129-136 -> :263-280). So a one-character ladder could only ever ladder that one character. Putting the models INTO the variant file makes the arrows the single navigation method and the seam stops mattering; no code change. ORDER IS MODEL-MAJOR: left/right walks one character up its speed ladder, then crosses into the next character. Tabs are clickable, so any cell is one click. TICKS IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT - it is SMEAR at 12/s, i.e. cell Sm12; a separate TICKS entry would duplicate a rung and re-introduce the character/speed confound this grid exists to remove. GALLOP holds dBPM 2 at every speed so its 6 s lap is speed-invariant (lap = 60/(dBPM x players-per-voice), no absolute-BPM term). GROOVE scatter is a PROPORTION of the cycle so its figure scales with speed for free. RAIN jitter is held at 45 ms ABSOLUTE - that is what rain IS as stored, and the resulting ring flags at high speed are real information, not noise. rev 1 (A/B/C references) and rev 2 (the smear-only speed ladder) are recoverable from git.",
  "rev": 3,
